Records customer receipts and vendor payments, linking them to invoices/bills and generating the corresponding journal entries.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Register manual or batch customer payments / vendor payments
Apply payments to one or multiple invoices (partial or full)
Bank transfer, cash, check, credit card payments
Payment reconciliation with bank statements
Refunds and payment returns
Payment registers and payment reports

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread + activity.mixin)
Key Fields:
payment_type (inbound/outbound)
partner_type (customer/supplier)
partner_id, amount (monetary), currency_id
journal_id → account.journal (required)
payment_method_id, payment_method_line_id
date, state (draft/posted/sent/reconciled/cancelled)
move_id → account.move (the journal entry it creates)
reconciled_invoice_ids / reconciled_bill_ids (Many2many)
ref, communication

Critical Hooks: action_post, action_draft, do_reconcile, _create_payment_entry, onchange_journal_id, compute_payment_difference
Security: account.group_account_user + company + journal rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
payment, customer payment, vendor payment, receipt, pay invoice, register payment, payment entry, inbound payment, outbound payment, payment reconciliation, payment journal, mass payment, payment register, draft payment, posted payment, reconciled payment, unreconciled payment, sent payment, payment state
Related Models (most joined):

account.move (created journal entry)
account.move.line (payment lines)
account.journal
res.partner
account.bank.statement.line
account.invoice (legacy) / reconciled moves
account.payment.method

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
account.payment is Odoo’s main model for recording inbound (customer) and outbound (vendor) payments with amount, journal, partner, payment method, and state. It automatically creates and posts account.move + account.move.line, handles multi-invoice allocation, partial payments, and reconciliation with bank statements. Central to the payment workflow and tightly integrated with accounting, bank, and invoicing modules.